  "english": "17. Monday. Tone 2 [PD / Bdz]. Fast of Advent. Fathers [Hymn]: \"God of our fathers, who saved\" (Harts'n merots astuats vor abretsuts'er).\n21. Friday. Tone 8 [DZ / Dzk]. Fast. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy Mother of God (Three Years Old).\n23. Sunday. Tone 1 [AD / Az]. First [Sunday of Advent]. Fathers [Hymn] Tone 1 [ad]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord God\" (Orhneal es ter astuats). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [ad]: \"With the women\" (End kanaysn) and \"Ineffable\" (Vor anch'ar).\n24. Monday. Tone 2 [AK / Ak]. [Feast of] Julian and Vasilouhi. Fathers [Hymn] Tone 2 [b]: \"Generous\" (Anokhagal).\n30. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK / Dzk]. Second [Sunday of Advent]. Fathers [Hymn] Tone 2 [ak]: \"Unoriginate Word\" (Anskizbn band). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [gk]: \"Thy angel, Lord\" (Hreshtak ko ter). And see the rest according to the order.\n\nDecember.\n1. Monday. Tone 1 [AD / Az]. [Feast of] Gennarius and Mercurius, and of Jacob and of Iravap'ar.\n2. Tuesday. Tone 2 [AK / Ak]. [Feast of] Cornelius the Centurion, and of Simeon, and the others.\n7. Sunday. Tone 8 [DZ / Dzk]. Third [Sunday of Advent]. Fathers [Hymn] Tone 3 [b3 / Bdz]: \"Incorruptible\" (Anapakankan). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [dձ3 / Dzd]: \"Who art above\" (Vor i verd es). Barekendan [Pre-fast] of the Fast of Saint James.\n9. Tuesday. Tone 7 [SD / Dzd]. Fast. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n10. Wednesday. Tone 2 [AK / Ak]. Fathers [Hymn] of the Fast, Tone 7 [d3 / Dzd]: \"Who for the three children\" (Vor zeris mankunsn).\n14. Sunday. Tone 6 [GK / Gk]. Fourth [Sunday of Advent]. Fathers [Hymn] Tone 4 [bk]: \"Unoriginate God\" (Anskizbn astuats). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [gk]: \"Resurrected and our\" (Ar'eal ev mer).\n21. Sunday. Tone 5 [GD / Gdz]. Fifth [Sunday of Advent]. Fathers [Hymn] Tone 5 [g3 / Gdz]: \"Glorified Son\" (P'ar'avoreal ordi). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [g3 / Gdz]: \"Myrrh-bearing\" (Yughaber), to the end.\n22. Monday. Tone 6 [GK / Gk]. [Feast of] Abraham and Khoren, Cosmas and Damian, and of Astuatsatour the Witness. Fathers [Hymn] Tone 7 [d3 / Dzd]: \"Those who trust\" (Yousats'ealk'n).\n23. Tuesday. Tone 8 [DZ / Dzk]. [Feast of] David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n28. Sunday. Tone 4 [BK / Bk]. Sixth [Sunday of Advent]. Fathers [Hymn] Tone 6 [gk]: \"Pre-eternal\" (Nakhahavitean). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [bk]: \"The women forestalled\" (Kankhets'in kanayk'n), to the end.\n29. Monday. Tone 7 [GD / Gdz]. [Feast of the] Sons of Thunder. Barekendan [Pre-fast] of the Fast of the Nativity.\n30. Tuesday. Tone 6 [GK / Gk]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. Fathers [Hymn] Tone 8 [dk]: \"Blessed art thou, [Lord] God of our fathers\" (Harts'n merots orhneal es).\n31. Wednesday. Tone 8 [DZ / Dzk]. Fast. Fathers [Hymn] Tone 8 [dk]: \"Blessed is the Lord God, blessed\" (Orhneal ter astuats orhneal). And the rest according to the order.\n\nJanuary.\n4. Sunday. Tone 3 [BZ / Bdz]. Seventh [Sunday of Advent]. Fast. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [b3 / Bdz]: \"Today they rejoiced\" (Aysor zuarch'ats'an), to the end.\n5. Monday. Tone 4 [BK / Bk]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ [Jragaluyts].\n\nThe Roman Weekly Cycle, 2.\n17. Thursday. [Feast of] Anton the Anchorite.\n19. Saturday. [Feast of] Theodosius the King, and of the Children of Ephesus.\n20. Sunday. First [Sunday after Epiphany]. Fathers [Hymn] Tone 7 [dz]: \"Dawning of the Only-Begotten\" (Tsagumn miatsni).\n21. Monday. [Feast of] Cyriacus and Jovita, and of Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris.\n\nJanuary.\n6. SUNDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The intervening period of leisure is nineteen days.\n14. Monday. [Feast of] John the Forerunner.\n15. Tuesday. [Feast of] Peter the Patriarch, Blaise, and the others.",
